    "title": "The History of Prospect Park, Brooklyn, NYC",
    "summary": "Prospect Park is a 585-acre urban oasis in the heart of Brooklyn, New York City. Designed by Frederick Law Olmsted and Calvert Vaux after their completion of Central Park, it is considered by many to be their masterpiece. Its history charts a course from ambitious civic project to decline and neglect, followed by a remarkable community-led revitalization that has restored it to its former glory.",
    "timeline": [
      {
        "period": "Conception and Design (1859-1866)",
